  "kind": "excel-differs-from-math",
  "title": "RRI runs the raw x87 EXP((1/nper)*LN(fv/pv)) - 1 chain (skipping nper == 1), drifting 298 ULP on RRI(96,10000,11000)",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0 builds 20228 through 20527, RRI(nper, pv, fv) rejects nper < DBL_MIN before checking pv == fv (with DAZ normalization, so equal negative pv and fv return +0), rejects pv == 0 or opposite nonzero signs with #NUM!, returns fv / pv - 1 directly at nper == 1, and otherwise evaluates exp(RN53(RN64((1 / nper) * ln(fv / pv)))) - 1 via the raw x87 chain (bypassing POWER's 0.5 sqrt shortcut). Subtracting 1 near 1 loses bits, putting =RRI(96,10000,11000) 298 ULP below exact. Under compat-1, @RRI returns #NAME?.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured in Excel 16.0 build 20228 (5,528/5,528 full-bank and 120/120 pinned RRI rows) and 16.0.20527.20088 in prefix_metadata (row 387).",
